msgid "Temperature"
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/wwand/graph.js:120
msgid ""
"The 3G counterpart to SINR: pilot energy against everything else in the "
"carrier. Above roughly -7 dB a connection starts to suffer; the steps drawn "
"here are the common operator convention around that figure, which is less "
"firmly published than the LTE and 5G ladders. On a modem that normally runs "
"LTE, this canvas appearing at all is the news."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/settings.js:1210
msgid ""
"The 3GPP usage setting the modem reports to the network: whether this device "
"is here for data or for voice. It is a preference, not a command — what the "
"network then does about voice continuity is its decision. Data centric is "
"what a router wants."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/status.js:934
msgid ""
"The 5G NR serving cell: band · centre frequency · bandwidth · Physical Cell "
"ID"
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/status.js:878
msgid ""
"The LTE/5G attach the modem performed, and the 3GPP cause when the network "
"refused it. Reported separately from registration because the two can fail "
"independently — a wrong attach APN registers fine and never attaches"
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/modems.js:396
msgid "The PUK must be exactly 8 digits."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/status.js:626
msgid ""
"The card reports itself busy. Reads of ICCID, IMSI and the PIN state will "
"fail until it clears, which is why those rows may be missing."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/modems.js:183
msgid ""
"The card the modem is using: its readiness, which physical slot is live, and "
"whether that slot holds an eUICC (eSIM)."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/wwand/simlist.js:123
msgid "The card's ICCID (printed on the SIM / shown on the modem status page)."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/settings.js:473
msgid ""
"The carrier profile (MBN) the modem applies: APN defaults, IMS settings, "
"band and roaming policy for a given network. The wrong one leaves the modem "
"technically working but subtly wrong on that network — a rejected attach, no "
"IMS, a missing band."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/modems.js:173
msgid ""
"The control protocol wwand speaks to this modem: QMI, MBIM or NCM. Set by "
"`option protocol`, or detected from the control device."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/modems.js:187
msgid ""
"The current signal, per radio technology. RSRP is reception strength, RSRQ "
"quality, SNR the noise margin — RSRP alone does not say whether the link is "
"good."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/modems.js:374
msgid ""
"The daemon refuses to auto-enter the PIN (%s) to protect the last attempts. "
"Enter the PIN to release it manually."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/wwand/graph.js:115
msgid ""
"The downlink bandwidth of the aggregated carriers added up, per radio "
"technology — the width of the pipe, which is what carrier aggregation is "
"for. It moves independently of the carrier count: three 10 MHz carriers are "
"less than one 20 MHz carrier. Drawn only where the modem reports a width per "
"carrier. The 5G line is usually absent for that reason: the 5G rows of the "
"carrier list carry a bandwidth whose unit this tree has not verified against "
"hardware, and a confidently wrong 100 MHz is worse than a gap."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/settings.js:70
msgid ""
"The eUICC refused to enable this profile: while a test profile is enabled, "
"only the profile that was active before it can be re-enabled (SGP.22 "
"\"wrongProfileReenabling\")."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/modems.js:168
msgid ""
"The kernel network device the modem's data runs on, with the model behind "
"it. A muxed connection names the child device (wwan0m1), not the parent."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/status.js:630
msgid ""
"The last thing the card said about itself: a session it closed and why, an "
"internal recovery, or an activation that did not complete."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/wwand/logbox.js:366
msgid ""
"The level the wwand PROCESS logs at — not a display filter. Takes effect at "
"once and is NOT written to the configuration: a restart or a config reload "
"returns to the configured level."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/wwand/graph.js:82
msgid ""
"The measure to aim an antenna by, and the same steps the router's signal "
"LEDs use: the serving cell's own power, RSRP on LTE and 5G, RSCP on 3G. LTE "
"and 5G NR are graded alike, because published tables give SSB-RSRP the same "
"boundaries as LTE RSRP below 6 GHz. RSSI is a different measure on its own "
"graph."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/settings.js:103
msgid "The modem did not answer in time."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/settings.js:99
msgid "The modem does not support that operation."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/wwand/esim.js:428
msgid ""
"The modem downloads over its own network attach — no router data path or APN "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/status.js:617
msgid ""
"The modem has not yet answered in the control protocol wwand is using, so no "
"hardware recovery step will run — repowering a modem that was never broken "
"only adds outages. Check the control protocol setting and the bound driver."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/status.js:542
msgid ""
"The modem has two independent radio switches. Software is the one wwand "
"controls and switches on at start-up; hardware is a physical switch or an "
"airplane-mode toggle on the host, which wwand cannot override — a modem held "
"off by it will not register no matter how often it is reset."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/settings.js:102
msgid "The modem is busy with another operation. Try again in a moment."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/status.js:576
msgid ""
"The modem is holding its own radio back — usually reduced transmit power. "
"This is the explanation for throughput that drops while the signal stays "
"good."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/settings.js:105
msgid "The modem is not ready yet."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/wwand/esim.js:76
msgid "The modem returned no profiles for this slot."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/status.js:197
msgid ""
"The modem serial port that carries NMEA sentences. wwand finds it during "
"enumeration; with wwand-gps installed it also reads it."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/settings.js:107
msgid ""
"The modem's current radio-technology setting does not allow a band list to "
"be written."
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/status.js:890
msgid ""
"The network currently serving the modem, as name (MCC/MNC). MCC = country, "
"MNC = network within it"
msgstr ""

#: applications/luci-app-wwand/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/wwand/modems.js:185
msgid ""
"The network the modem is registered on, or why it is not. A reject cause "
"here is the network refusing, not the modem failing."
msgstr ""

