"interference. Coarser than RSRP and graded 20 dB higher (-65/-75/-85 dBm), "
"which is why it has its own graph: a strong signal reaches -46 dBm, off the "
"top of any scale drawn for RSRP. On 2G it is the only measure there is, and "
"on a modem that reports nothing better it is all you get. Each line carries "
"the radio that measured it; the plain amber one appears only when the reply "
"is untagged."
